WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.944
This session teaches all five saved sections of the school APGAR module as topic-matched support for the explicit newborn practical. It is not an invented school allocation.
本节把学校APGAR模块全部五节用于明确新生儿实操的主题配套，不捏造学校周次安排。

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:20.616
The skill is a consistent timed description and useful communication. The score is not a replacement for immediate assessment of breathing and heart rate.
技能是统一定时描述及有效沟通。分数不能替代即时呼吸心率评估。

00:00:20.616 --> 00:00:29.544
We will learn the components before interpreting the total. Knowing what produced a number is more useful than reciting only eight out of ten.
需先学构成再解释总分。知道数字如何组成，比只背十分中八分有用。

00:00:29.544 --> 00:00:40.296
The examples are original scoring exercises and not answers to the school quiz. Actual neonatal resuscitation decisions belong to the separate current algorithm session.
例子为原创评分练习，不是学校测验答案。真实新生儿复苏决定属于独立现行算法节。

00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:51.600
Virginia Apgar developed the system in the early nineteen-fifties and published it in nineteen fifty-three. The later acronym is a memory aid, not five separate diagnoses.
Virginia Apgar在二十世纪五十年代初制定、于一九五三发表系统。之后的缩写是记忆辅助，不是五个独立诊断。

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:59.112
Its strength is a common vocabulary for describing a newborn at a specified time and reporting a change after support.
其优势是共同词汇，可描述指定时间新生儿及支持后变化。

00:00:59.112 --> 00:01:10.944
The five observations include color, heart rate, reflex response, tone and breathing effort. Some are subjective and all must be related to the real clinical context.
五观察包括颜色、心率、反射、张力及呼吸用力，部分主观，全部都需联系真实背景。

00:01:10.944 --> 00:01:24.072
A historical origin does not mean every old treatment recommendation remains current. Scoring principles and an old resuscitation algorithm must not be treated as one inseparable document.
历史来源不代表旧治疗建议都仍现行，评分原则与旧复苏算法不能当不可分同一文件。

00:01:24.072 --> 00:01:36.072
The school uses triage-tag imagery for the score ranges, but that can be misleading if interpreted literally. Treatment must not wait for the total or be selected solely from its color band.
学校用分诊标签比喻范围，照字面理解会误导。治疗不能等总分，也不能只按颜色带选择。

00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:45.864
A newborn who is apneic needs immediate appropriate care before the one-minute score is due. A total alone cannot decide whether compressions are indicated.
无呼吸婴儿在一分钟评分到时前就需适当即时照护，总分本身不能决定按压适应证。

00:01:45.864 --> 00:01:55.704
The same total can come from different component combinations and different support. State the observations and use the current newborn pathway for action.
相同总分可来自不同构成与不同支持。需说观察，并以现行新生儿路径决定行动。

00:01:55.704 --> 00:02:06.648
A reassuring-looking total does not override poor breathing, a new clinical change or an unreliable measurement. Continue direct assessment and reassessment.
看似放心总分不能推翻呼吸差、新临床变或测量不可靠，需持续直接评估复评。

00:02:06.648 --> 00:02:18.024
Record the complete-birth time and use it as the timing reference. Time of calling dispatch, head delivery or cord cutting is not automatically the baby's age clock.
需记录完整出生时间并作为计时参考。呼叫派遣、头出或剪脐时间，不自动等于出生年龄时钟。

00:02:18.024 --> 00:02:30.288
Assign the one- and five-minute observations at the appropriate times while necessary care continues. Do not wait until stabilization and then label the later condition as the earlier score.
必要照护继续时，需在合适时间评一分及五分观察。不能等稳定后把晚状态标为早分数。

00:02:30.288 --> 00:02:41.568
When a precise scheduled observation was missed, document the actual time and available information honestly. Do not invent a retrospective normal score to fill a form.
漏准确预定观察时，需如实记真实时间及可用资料，不能事后编正常分填表。

00:02:41.568 --> 00:02:50.088
Use a team member for timing and documentation when resources permit. That allows the treatment provider to continue effective support.
资源许可时可分人计时记录，让治疗者持续有效支持。

00:02:50.088 --> 00:03:04.848
The school introduction says seven or less, while its glossary says less than seven. The selected AAP statement and the textbook support less than seven at five minutes for repeated five-minute scoring up to twenty minutes.
学校介绍写七或以下，术语表写低于七。所选AAP声明及教材支持五分钟低于七时，每五分钟重复至二十分钟。

00:03:04.848 --> 00:03:15.912
A scheduled scoring interval is not permission to reassess the patient only every five minutes. Breathing and heart-rate decisions remain continuous and time-sensitive.
预定评分间隔不允许每五分钟才看一次患者，呼吸心率决定仍持续且时间敏感。

00:03:15.912 --> 00:03:24.888
Reaching seven does not automatically end all clinical monitoring, and reaching twenty minutes does not independently direct cessation of treatment.
达到七不自动结束全部临床监测，到二十分钟也不独立指示停止治疗。

00:03:24.888 --> 00:03:37.008
Do not use the old ten-minute-zero discussion as a field termination rule. Current resuscitation decisions need the actual guideline, consultation, clinical context and family communication.
不能把旧十分零分讨论当现场终止规则。现行复苏决定需真实指导、会诊、临床背景及家庭沟通。

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:48.744
Each component receives zero, one or two points, and the total ranges from zero to ten. Keep the component order consistent so nothing is omitted or counted twice.
每项零、一或二分，总零至十。需保持顺序一致，避免遗漏或重复。

00:03:48.744 --> 00:03:59.760
Use observed findings at the time point. A treatment plan, a likely future improvement or the fact that someone is ventilating does not supply a spontaneous normal finding.
需用该时点所见。计划、预期好转或有人正在通气，都不能提供自发正常发现。

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:08.640
Separate observation from interpretation. Record the actual rate or response as well as the component score when useful for the handover.
需分观察与解释，交接有用时应同时记真实频率反应及分项。

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:18.312
If a component cannot be assessed reliably, use the applicable documentation process and disclose the limitation rather than guess a flattering total.
某项不能可靠评时，应依适用记录流程说明限制，不能猜漂亮总分。

00:04:18.312 --> 00:04:29.616
The conventional appearance chart gives zero for an entirely blue or pale appearance, one for central color with peripheral cyanosis and two for the chart's entirely pink description.
传统颜色表为全身蓝或苍白零分、中央颜色可而外周蓝一分、表中全粉红描述二分。

00:04:29.616 --> 00:04:41.520
Do not interpret natural pigmentation as cyanosis or subtract points because a baby does not literally have pale pink skin. Assess appropriate central sites and document uncertainty.
不能把自然肤色当发绀，也不能因不呈浅粉皮就扣分。需看合适中央部位并记不确定。

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:54.024
Acrocyanosis affects hands and feet and can occur during transition; persistent central cyanosis or pallor has a different meaning. Neither should be interpreted from skin color alone in poor lighting.
肢端发绀影响手足，可见于过渡；持续中央发绀或苍白意义不同。光差时都不能只凭皮色解释。

00:04:54.024 --> 00:05:04.968
Use reliable oxygenation and the clinical assessment for treatment decisions. Do not invent a race-based numerical correction or let the appearance score replace monitoring.
治疗需依可靠氧合及临床评，不能造种族数字修正，也不能让颜色分代监测。

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:14.424
The school's detailed criterion gives zero when no heartbeat is detected, one for a present rate below one hundred, and two for one hundred or more.
学校详细标准为无可测心搏零分、有但低于一百一分、一百及以上二分。

00:05:14.424 --> 00:05:23.808
That avoids the old textbook table's unassigned exactly-one-hundred boundary. It does not mean a pulse of one hundred alone proves a healthy transition.
这避免旧教材表中恰好一百未分配的边界，但不表示仅脉一百就证明健康过渡。

00:05:23.808 --> 00:05:33.696
Use a reliable method and communicate the measured rate. Do not spend a full minute delaying necessary support solely to resolve an urgent rate estimate.
需可靠方法并报实测速率，不能只为解急心率估计而用整分钟延误必要支持。

00:05:33.696 --> 00:05:43.752
Apgar pulse points are not compression thresholds. The current newborn algorithm includes effectiveness and duration of ventilation before its compression decision.
Apgar脉分不是按压阈值，现行新生儿算法在按压决定前还包含通气有效性及时间。

00:05:43.752 --> 00:05:54.264
Assess reflex irritability through an appropriate gentle stimulus such as necessary drying or rubbing the back. Observe what the baby actually does.
需通过必要擦干或轻揉背等适当轻柔刺激评反射，并观察真实反应。

00:05:54.264 --> 00:06:04.056
No response scores zero, a grimace or weak response one, and a vigorous response such as a strong cry, cough or sneeze two under the school chart.
依学校表，无反应零、皱眉弱反应一、强哭咳或喷嚏等有力反应二。

00:06:04.056 --> 00:06:16.152
Do not perform unnecessary deep suction, slap, shake or repeatedly flick the baby to elicit a higher score. The assessment must not create injury or delay ventilation.
不能为较高分做多余深吸、打、摇或反复弹婴。评估不能造伤或延误通气。

00:06:16.152 --> 00:06:26.544
Describe the stimulus and response when useful. A reflex score alone does not diagnose neurological damage or explain why the response is reduced.
有用时需描述刺激与反应。单独反射分不诊神经损伤，也不解释反应降低原因。

00:06:26.544 --> 00:06:36.048
Observe posture and spontaneous movement. Limpness, some flexion and active movement with good flexion represent different component findings.
需看姿势及自发活动。松软、部分屈曲、活动与屈曲良好代表不同分项。

00:06:36.048 --> 00:06:45.696
Assign zero for limpness, one for some flexion or limited activity and two for active movement and good flexion according to the school criteria.
依学校标准，松软零、部分屈曲或有限活动一、活动及屈曲良好二。

00:06:45.696 --> 00:06:58.344
Prematurity, medication exposure, illness and injury can affect tone. Do not equate a low tone point with a single diagnosis or ignore it simply because the infant is preterm.
早产、药物暴露、病及伤可影响张力。不能把低张力分等同一个诊断，也不能因早产就忽视。

00:06:58.344 --> 00:07:07.872
Note asymmetry or a new change as a separate clinical finding. Do not force painful limb extension merely to prove resistance for the score.
不对称或新变需另作临床发现，不能只为证明抵抗而强痛伸肢。

00:07:07.872 --> 00:07:21.744
Observe spontaneous breathing effort and listen for the cry. Zero indicates absent breathing, one slow or irregular effort or weak cry, and two good effort with a strong cry in the school description.
需观察自发呼吸用力并听哭。学校描述无呼吸零，慢不齐或弱哭一，良好用力强哭二。

00:07:21.744 --> 00:07:30.816
A chest rise produced by positive-pressure ventilation is not automatically evidence of spontaneous respiration worth two points.
正压通气制造胸起，不自动代表值二分的自发呼吸。

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:42.312
Do not interrupt necessary effective ventilation merely to obtain an unassisted score. Use concurrent observations and the applicable assisted-documentation process.
不能只为取得无辅助分数而中断必要有效通气。需用同时观察及适用辅助记录流程。

00:07:42.312 --> 00:07:53.280
Regardless of the points, inadequate breathing needs the current newborn pathway now. Do not wait for the total or keep stimulating a baby whose ventilation is failing.
无论分数，呼吸不足现在就需现行新生儿路径，不能等总分或对通气失败者一直刺激。

00:07:53.280 --> 00:08:01.896
The school section telling you to stop ventilation to assess breathing should not be treated as a routine instruction to interrupt life-saving support.
学校要求停通气评呼吸的段落，不能当成常规中断救命支持指令。

00:08:01.896 --> 00:08:10.176
Document the support actually occurring at the time point along with observations and component scores, using the approved reporting format.
应按批准格式在时点旁记真实支持、观察及分项。

00:08:10.176 --> 00:08:22.032
A score obtained during assisted breathing is not equivalent to one in a spontaneously breathing infant. Do not silently compare totals as though the circumstances were identical.
辅助呼吸中分数不等于自发呼吸儿分数，不能默默当情境相同地比较总数。

00:08:22.032 --> 00:08:32.568
If information is unavailable, disclose it and record what is known. Do not manufacture a complete perfect score or interrupt necessary support to remove uncertainty.
资料缺时需说明并记已知，不能编完整完美分，也不能为消除未知而中断必要支持。

00:08:32.568 --> 00:08:42.120
Use a consistent order and a clear time reference. Two people assessing different moments may be describing real change rather than one being wrong.
需一致顺序及清时间。两人评不同时刻，可能是真变化，不一定一人错。

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:54.192
When scores differ, compare specific component observations and the support underway. A statement such as the total looks too low is not a reason to alter documented findings.
分数不同时需比具体分项及正在支持。觉得总分太低，不是改已记发现的理由。

00:08:54.192 --> 00:09:04.848
Acknowledge subjective elements and improve light, technique or information when feasible. Do not use confidence or seniority as a substitute for evidence.
需承认主观项，并可行时改善光技术资料，不能用自信或资历代证据。

00:09:04.848 --> 00:09:15.144
Continue effective care while discrepancies are clarified. The purpose is reliable communication, not winning a scoring argument during resuscitation.
澄差异时仍持续有效照护，目的是可靠沟通，不是在复苏时赢评分争论。

00:09:15.144 --> 00:09:26.352
The school describes seven to ten, four to six and zero to three. The selected professional statement places these descriptors in the five-minute term and late-preterm context.
学校描述七至十、四至六及零至三，所选专业声明将这些描述置于五分钟足月及晚期早产背景。

00:09:26.352 --> 00:09:39.312
These ranges summarize condition but do not select a universal package of suction, oxygen or compressions. The underlying observations and current algorithm determine what is needed.
范围概括状态，却不能选一套通用吸引、给氧或按压。真实观察及现行算法决定需要。

00:09:39.312 --> 00:09:50.352
A high total does not prove every component is normal, and a low total does not prove asphyxia. State the time, components, support and clinical concern.
高总分不证明每项正常，低总分不证明窒息。需说时间、构成、支持及担忧。

00:09:50.352 --> 00:09:59.088
Do not guarantee improvement by five minutes or cease observation because a target score was reached. Reassess the actual trajectory.
不能保证五分前改善，也不能因达到目标分就停止观察，需评真实趋势。

00:09:59.088 --> 00:10:08.808
A preterm infant may score differently because of immaturity. That does not prove asphyxia or mean that current inadequate breathing needs no treatment.
早产儿可因未成熟而分不同，这不证明窒息，也不代表当前呼吸不足不用治。

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:19.728
Maternal medicines and several illnesses can alter tone, responsiveness or breathing. The score records the condition but cannot identify the cause alone.
母体药物及多病可改变张力、反应或呼吸，分数记状态，却不能单独识因。

00:10:19.728 --> 00:10:29.400
Observer differences, lighting and treatment can change apparent findings. Interpret a trend with the circumstances, not only the arithmetic.
观察者、光线及治疗可改表面发现，解释趋势需结合情境，不只算术。

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:41.472
Avoid racial or clinical bias by assessing and documenting actual components. No appearance adjustment should substitute for an appropriate objective oxygenation and clinical assessment.
需通过真实分项评记避免种族临床偏差，不能用外观调整替代合适客观氧合及临床评。

00:10:41.472 --> 00:10:51.552
Lower scores can be associated with worse outcomes across populations. An association does not let you predict the future neurological function of one infant.
人群低分可与较差结局相关，但关联不能让你预测某婴未来神经功能。

00:10:51.552 --> 00:11:03.960
A low score is nonspecific and cannot independently establish birth asphyxia. More clinical and laboratory information is needed to assess impaired gas exchange and its cause.
低分非特异，不能独立证明出生窒息；评气体交换障碍及原因需更多临床化验资料。

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:14.160
Do not tell families that a low score guarantees disability or a higher score guarantees no injury. Explain what is being observed and what support is underway.
不能向家属说低分保证残疾、高分保证无伤。应解释所见及正在提供的支持。

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:24.864
Use current consultation and team decision processes for serious resuscitation questions. The number must not become a standalone decision to withhold or stop care.
严重复苏问题需现行会诊团队决定，数字不能成为独立不开始或停止照护决定。

00:11:24.864 --> 00:11:37.416
This original scoring example has central color with blue hands and feet, heart rate ninety, a weak grimace, some limb flexion and weak irregular spontaneous breathing at one minute.
原创评分例在一分钟为中央颜色可、手足蓝，心率九十、弱皱眉、部分屈曲及弱不齐自发呼吸。

00:11:37.416 --> 00:11:46.008
Each observation earns one point in the school chart, so the total is five. State all components rather than only the total.
依学校表各一分，总五。应说全部构成，不只总数。

00:11:46.008 --> 00:11:56.664
Necessary support is already underway according to the newborn pathway. We did not wait to calculate five before responding to the breathing and heart-rate findings.
所需支持已依新生儿路径开始，不是等算出五分才响应呼吸心率发现。

00:11:56.664 --> 00:12:07.728
Record the time and concurrent support, and continue reassessment. This one-minute total does not determine a prognosis or automatically select chest compressions.
需记时间及同时支持并继续复评。一分钟总数不定预后，也不自动选按压。

00:12:07.728 --> 00:12:20.424
Now assume a measured rate of one hundred thirty-six, vigorous response, active flexion and a strong spontaneous cry at five minutes, with blue hands and feet still present.
现假设五分钟心率实测一百三十六、反应强、活动屈曲好、自发强哭，但手足仍蓝。

00:12:20.424 --> 00:12:29.352
The score is one plus two plus two plus two plus two, totaling nine. Do not increase appearance to two merely to produce ten.
分为一加二加二加二加二，总九。不能只为凑十而把颜色改二。

00:12:29.352 --> 00:12:41.064
Report how support and observations changed between time points. If support remains, document it; an improving total does not erase the care required to obtain that condition.
需报两时点支持及观察变化，仍有支持就记。总分改善不能抹去达到状态所需照护。

00:12:41.064 --> 00:12:51.288
Continue appropriate newborn monitoring and warmth. A total of nine is not an independent discharge, transport-refusal or long-term-outcome clearance.
需继续适当婴监测保暖。九分不是独立出院、拒运或远期结局保证。

00:12:51.288 --> 00:13:02.496
Start with complete-birth time, estimated gestation and the infant's current age. State when each score was assigned and whether timing was exact or estimated.
需先完整出生时间、估孕周及当前年龄，再说各评分时间及是否精确。

00:13:02.496 --> 00:13:13.512
Give the total with relevant component details and measured heart rate. Explain limitations such as uncertain color or unavailable spontaneous observations during support.
需给总数及相关构成与实测心率，并解释颜色不确定或支持时自发观察缺失等限制。

00:13:13.512 --> 00:13:25.584
Report ventilation, oxygen, airway support, compressions or medicines actually given, with time and response. Do not imply unsupported recovery when the infant remains assisted.
需报真实通气、给氧、气道、按压或药的时间反应。婴仍需辅助时，不能暗示无支持恢复。

00:13:25.584 --> 00:13:33.768
Finish with the current clinical concern and transfer needs. The score supports the story; it is not the entire handover.
最后需当前临床担忧及转移需求。分数支持故事，不是全部交接。

00:13:33.768 --> 00:13:42.264
You should now describe each component and calculate an original example without changing observations to fit a desired total.
现在应能描述每项并算原创例，不为想要总数而改变观察。

00:13:42.264 --> 00:13:52.848
Use the actual birth clock and document time-specific support. Resolve the school less-than-seven inconsistency without turning a scoring interval into a treatment delay.
需用真实出生时钟并记时点支持，解决学校低于七不一致，但不能把评分间隔变治疗延误。

00:13:52.848 --> 00:14:02.952
Never stop necessary ventilation merely to obtain a pure score. Current breathing and heart-rate findings guide care independently of the arithmetic.
不能只为纯分数停止必要通气。当前呼吸心率独立于算术指导照护。

00:14:02.952 --> 00:14:13.104
Keep the limits visible when communicating with clinicians and families. Accurate modest interpretation is more useful than a confident unsupported prediction.
对临床及家属沟通时需保限制，准确有分寸解释比确信无据预测更有用。
